findings.proposed_fix:
New file Sources/Qnet/NetworkArchetypes.swift holding three plain value types and one builder, and a new sheet Sources/Qnet/ArchetypeGallerySheet.swift.

(1) Data model — no Codable, no persistence, nothing the exporters can see:
  enum NetworkArchetype: String, CaseIterable, Identifiable { case tandemLine, openJacksonFeedback, mmcStation, reentrantTwoStation, forkStyleSplit, machineRepair, callCentre }
  struct ArchetypeParameters { var stations = 3; var servers = 1; var targetRho = 0.9; var feedbackProbability = 0.3; var infiniteBuffers = true; var bufferCapacity = 10; var arrivalRate = 1.0 }
  struct ArchetypeBlueprint { let id: NetworkArchetype; let title: String; let subtitle: String /* "Src → B1 → S1 → … → Sink" */; let systemImage: String /* DS.Symbol.* only */; let knobs: Set<Knob>; let provenance: String? /* "same shape as input/examples/3dtandem.inf.bnet" */ }

(2) Builder: `@MainActor enum NetworkArchetypeBuilder { static func build(_:_:origin:) -> RandomNetworkGenerator.Result }`. Reuse RandomNetworkGenerator.Result (RandomNetworkGenerator.swift:53-57) verbatim so no new type crosses into the editor, and reuse its layout constants (xRowStart 200, xStep 130, yRow 220, RandomNetworkGenerator.swift:68-74) so an archetype lands laid out identically to a generated network. Every archetype emits the mandatory Buffer-before-Station pairing SRBMExporter enforces (SRBMExporter.swift:98-112). Rates are back-solved the way the bundled examples are built: μ_i = λ / (ρ_target · c_i), which reproduces exactly the ρ = 0.9 / E[N] = 9 shape validation/example_contracts.py already asserts, so a dropped tandem is immediately stable, runnable, and hits the exact-Jackson branch of AnalyticalTractability.swift:71.

(3) Insertion — one new method on NetworkEditorModel, next to pasteClipboardContents:
  @discardableResult func insertSubnetwork(nodes:links:infiniteBuffers:at origin:actionName:) -> Set<UUID>
  It must, in this order: call performMutation(actionName) (NetworkEditorModel.swift:2300) so the snapshot — which already carries stationCount/bufferCount/sourceCount/sinkCount (NetworkSnapshot, 2246-2254) — makes the whole insert one undo step with correct name restoration; re-prime the four counters with max(counter, maxNameIndex(...)) exactly as pasteClipboardContents does (719-722); rename incoming nodes and rebuild their ids through the same idMap loop (724-770) so an insert into a non-empty canvas cannot collide; offset positions past the existing content bounds; set the inserted nodes as the selection via setNodeSelection (479); apply infiniteBuffers when the blueprint specifies it; call noteParametersChanged() (1049) so hasBeenAnalyzed resets and the flag bar re-runs; and addStatus the archetype name and its parameters.

(4) Presentation: ArchetypeGallerySheet cloned structurally from PicturePickerSheet (PicturePickerSheet.swift:43-101) — DSSheet + DSSheetHeader + sectioned LazyVGrid + arrow keys + double-click to choose — with the right-hand knob form built from the same DSNumericField/LabeledContent rows GenerateRandomNetworkSheet uses (NetworkDialogs.swift:60-126) and a DSSheetFooter carrying the first blocking problem. Wire `@State private var showArchetypeSheet` exactly like showGenerateRandomSheet (QnetGUIApp.swift:552, 745-753) and add it to appSheetPresented (QnetGUIApp.swift:1587). Entry points: File ▸ New from Template… beside Open Example… (QnetCommands.swift:227), Network ▸ Insert Archetype… beside Generate Random Network… (QnetCommands.swift:729), and the canvas empty-state action button.
